"""Make the Apple AVE encoder's firmware files for this Mac, verify them, install them.

No Apple firmware or data taken from Apple's files is shipped with
apple-ave. Everything the driver needs is made here, on the user's machine,
from the user's own copy of Apple's files:

  apple/ave_<variant>.bin        the encoder firmware: the payload of
                                 Firmware/ave/AppleAVE2FW_<variant>.im4p
  apple/ave-13.5-dpe-<set>.bin   the AVE_DPE register tunables macOS applies,
                                 read from AppleAVE2.kext in a kernelcache
                                 (ave_fwgen.py)
  apple/ave-13.5-h13g-data-pristine.bin
                                 (M1 only) the firmware's DATA as the boot
                                 loader leaves it, built from the image

Where Apple's files come from, in this order:

  * the Asahi installer's copy of this Mac's kernelcache on the EFI system
    partition (asahi/kernelcache.release.*), when it is the 13.5 one;
  * --from-dir DIR: a directory holding the files, such as a mounted macOS
    13.5 Preboot volume (Asahi's stub included) or a copy of one;
  * --ipsw FILE: a local copy of Apple's macOS 13.5 (22G74) restore image;
  * by default, that image on Apple's CDN, read in place with HTTP range
    requests, as Asahi Linux's installer does: only the members needed
    (about 0.5 MB, and about 26 MB for the kernelcache unless the EFI
    partition has it), never the 13 GB image.

Every input and output is checked against known-hashes.txt (sha256) before
anything is written. A file that does not match is not installed.

The pristine DATA blob for the other SoCs is not in any file the user has:
the boot loader writes part of it. The driver keeps it at the first start
of each boot and offers it in debugfs; --capture checks it against the
image and installs it (ave-load does that after loading the driver).

Usage:
  apple-ave-fetch-firmware                 detect the SoC, show the plan, ask, install
  apple-ave-fetch-firmware --dry-run       show the plan only (no network, no writes)
  apple-ave-fetch-firmware --yes           do not ask (for automation)
  apple-ave-fetch-firmware --check         report what is installed (exit 1 if incomplete)
  apple-ave-fetch-firmware --capture       install the pristine DATA the driver kept
  apple-ave-fetch-firmware --ipsw FILE     read a local IPSW instead of the CDN
  apple-ave-fetch-firmware --from-dir DIR  search DIR for the files
  apple-ave-fetch-firmware --output-dir D  write into D instead of /lib/firmware (no root)

Exit status: 0 done (or nothing to do), 1 error, 2 usage, 3 declined.
"""
